+| **AuthScheme** | Auth / OpenAPI | NARROW security-scheme input to `auth(name, mw, scheme?)` — union `http bearer/basic` or `apiKey {in:`header`|`query`, name}` (unchanged since v0.5.4). When `auth(name,mw)` is registered WITHOUT a `scheme`, a default `{type:"http",scheme:"bearer"}` is published (issue #03) so a `{auth}` route is always documented protected. Keeping it narrow means an exhaustive switch over it stays valid even as the library emits more scheme kinds. |
+| **SecurityScheme** | Auth / OpenAPI | WIDE emitted type of `components.securitySchemes` — `AuthScheme | apiKey {in:`cookie`, name} | oauth2 {flows.authorizationCode}`. Use it when *reading* the emitted spec; use `AuthScheme` when *passing* a scheme to `auth()`. |
+| **AuthStrategy** | Auth | Handle returned by `auth.session/jwt/oauth/strategy(name, opts)` — groups a guard middleware (optional), an OpenAPI scheme, and flow helpers. Strategies are opt-in and register through the same path as `auth(name,mw,scheme?)`. |
+| **SessionStrategy** | Auth | Cookie-session strategy: signed `sid.hmac` cookie + pluggable `SessionStore`; guard yields the session payload as `req.auth`. Helpers: `create(c,data)` (sets cookie AND returns the `Set-Cookie` value), `destroy(c)`, `get(c)`, `generateCsrf(c)`, `verifyCsrf(c, token)`. |
+| **JwtStrategy** | Auth | HS256 access-token + opaque rotating refresh-token strategy; guard verifies the `Bearer` access token. Helpers: `issue(sub,claims?)`, `refresh(refreshToken)`, `revoke(refreshToken)`, `verifyAccess(token)`. Refresh tokens are single-use & family-revoked on reuse. |
+| **OAuthStrategy** | Auth | Google authorization-code + PKCE flow; emits an `oauth2` scheme, mounts `/start`+`/callback`. Helpers: `authorizeUrl(state, codeChallenge?)`, `exchangeCode(code, verifier?)`, `getUser(tokens)`, `mount(app)`. `onSuccess` is the only integration point. |
+| **SessionStore** | Auth | `get/set/delete(sid)` abstraction for the session payload. In-memory adapter: `createMemorySessionStore()`. |
+| **RefreshTokenStore** | Auth | `get/save/delete/getFamily/deleteFamily()` abstraction keyed by token hash. In-memory adapter: `createMemoryRefreshTokenStore()`. |
 | **ArkType** | Validation | `Type<any,any>` alias with callable validation `schema(data)=>data\|ArkErrors` and `toJsonSchema()`. Peer dep `arktype@^2.2.1`. |
 | **ArktypeValidator** | Validation | `validator(target, fn)` middleware factory that runs `coerceDeep` then `schema(data)` and **throws `APIError(400)`** on `ArkErrors` (never returns `Response`). |
 | **Coercion** | Validation | `coerceDeep(schema,data)`/`coerceValue(prop,raw,defs)` deep walk via `JsonSchema` translating query/header strings → numbers/booleans/arrays before validation; preserves `undefined`/empty-string for 400. Handles nested objects, `number[]` single-wrap, `boolean "true"/"false"` strictly. **Header invariant:** Hono lowercases incoming header keys via Fetch `Headers`; `coerceDeep` does NOT auto-lowercase — declare `type({ "x-api-key": "string" })` not `"X-Api-Key"` (strict fail-fast 400). Proposed `src/validation.ts`. |
 | **OapiPath** | OpenAPI | OpenAPI form `/{param}` derived via `toOapiPath(path)` — `:x`→`{x}`, `:x{regex}`→`{x}`, `:x?`→`{x}`, `*`→`{wildcard}`. `src/paths.ts` pure; header lowercasing is NOT here (see Coercion/ArktypeValidator ponytail — `_addObjectParams`). Used as `paths` key. |
 | **OperationId** | OpenAPI | Unique per operation; default `method_oapiPath` (`/`→`_`, `{}` stripped). Custom via `config.operationId`; dedup suffix `_2`,`_3` via `seenOperationIds:Set` + `baseCounts:Map`. |
-| **ComponentRegistry** | OpenAPI | `{schemas:Map<string,JsonSchema>, securitySchemes:Map<string,AuthScheme>}` hoisting `$defs` to stable names. |
+| **ComponentRegistry** | OpenAPI | `{schemas:Map<string,JsonSchema>, securitySchemes:Map<string,SecurityScheme>}` hoisting `$defs` to stable names. |
 | **Stable hash name** | OpenAPI | `schema_<sha1Hex(normalizeRefs(JSON.stringify(def))).slice(0,12)>` — content-hash over normalized structure, not ArkType counter `intersection216`. Via Web Crypto SHA-1. |
 | **RewriteRefs** | OpenAPI | Recursive in-place `#/$defs/X` → `#/components/schemas/schema_<hash>` rewriting (`rewriteRefs(node,rename)`). Handles objects + arrays. |
 | **DocsMount** | OpenAPI | `docs(specPath,uiPath)` binding — `app.doc(specPath,{openapi:"3.0.0",info})` + `app.get(uiPath, apiReference({spec:{url:specPath}}))`. Overload `(specPath?,uiPath?)` or `({specPath?,uiPath?})`. The spec builds **lazily** on the `/openapi.json` request; what matters for correctness is **route registration order** (Hono matches in order), so call `docs()` after route imports for clarity. |
